    "summary": "Hartford ’82 delivers a high‑energy set – scorching Shakedown, tight Lost Sailor, soaring Baby Blue.",
    "review": "The April 17, 1982 Hartford Civic Center gig is one of those spring‑time fireworks that still feels fresh. The band bursts out of the gate and by the second set they’re on an express‑train roll: a monster Shakedown Street launches into a razor‑sharp Lost Sailor > Saint of Circumstance, then blossoms into a soaring Spanish Jam that melts into space before landing cleanly on Uncle John’s Band. Jerry’s guitar is crisp and playful – riff trades with Brent sparkle, his vocal delivery on Baby Blue (the encore) hits right in the heart. Brent Mydland’s keyboards are the secret sauce all night, from trippy textures on The Other One to a big‑room piano lead that fuels the jams. Phil lays down a solid, sometimes under‑mixed bass foundation that still drives the improvisations, while Bill’s drum space is described as “beautiful,” giving the music room to breathe. Bob Weir’s vocals are passionate throughout, especially on Bird Song and the final Baby Blue, rounding out a show that feels locked in from start to finish.",
